#X text 20 1820 Steps are cut from c_clock's beat phase times four \, never from its beat bang \, which tops out at 14.3 a second (ref/module/tempo.md). The threshold is a twelfth of a step \, where u_tempo's MIDI pulse for that sixteenth falls \, so a step and the clock the 404 follows land in one block. Debounces 0 \, as in c_clock., f 58;
#X text 20 2010 Every track reads this one counter. Per-track subdivision would give each track its own multiplier on the same phase in place of the times four \, and its own counter., f 58;
#X text 300 670 PLAY starts at step 1: the counter parks at 15 so the next is 0. The spigot shuts for one logical instant \, so a step cut before c_clock's phase reset cannot fire as step 1. STOP and panic stop it and put the playhead out., f 44;
#X text 520 1280 One step plays every track not at 0 in one logical instant: m_404's budget passes sixteen at once and drops beyond that \, never queues (ref/device/sp404.md). A rest is moses' left outlet \, unconnected., f 44;
#X text 640 880 The step rule in one comparison: an off step is 0 and no level is \, so equal means turn it off and anything else means take the level., f 44;
#X text 1300 860 Level n is 127n/16 rounded: 8 at 1 \, 127 at 16. At load: level 13 \, 103 \, and track 1 \, so the page has a selection before anything is pressed., f 20;
#X text 1300 1360 The pattern is one auto key \, section-1-<part>: 256 velocities \, track by track (ref/module/state.md). A restore is put straight back: a load never fills u_state's live store \, so a key nobody re-puts is dropped at the next flush \, and a short or malformed line is repaired by the same put., f 50;
#X text 2100 1150 The bank's two pad offsets: a track's pad is its number plus (bank-1)*16., f 30;
#X text 1900 650 The reject is a real error: u_map and this file disagree about the vocabulary. C-8, f 26;
